      "data": {
        "passage": "In a bid to create a more inclusive environment, a local cinema has introduced relaxed Sunday screenings, catering to those who may find traditional cinema settings overwhelming. These special showings allow audiences to enjoy films in a more comfortable atmosphere, with adjustments such as reduced volume levels, dimmed lighting, and the freedom to move around or make noise. \n\nThe initiative aims to support individuals with sensory sensitivities, autism, or anxiety, as well as families with young children. By providing a welcoming space, the cinema hopes to encourage more people to experience the joy of film without the pressure of adhering to conventional cinema etiquette. \n\nFeedback from the community has been overwhelmingly positive, with many expressing gratitude for the opportunity to enjoy movies in a relaxed setting. This innovative approach not only enhances accessibility but also fosters a sense of belonging among diverse audiences, proving that cinema can be a shared experience for everyone.",
